# Driver app structure & conventions

## Target shape (evolve toward; avoid big-bang moves)

| Area | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/app/` | Routes, `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`; API in `app/api/**/route.ts` |
| `src/app/(driver)/` | Optional route group for driver-only shell vs other surfaces |
| `src/components/ui/` | Reusable primitives (Button, Modal) |
| `src/components/layout/` | Shells: `AuthGuard`, headers, `BrandLogo` |
| `src/features/<feature>/` | Optional: colocate `components/`, `hooks/`, `utils/` per product area |
| `src/hooks/` | Shared hooks |
| `src/lib/` | Auth helpers, domain logic, constants, socket clients |
| `src/stores/` | Zustand for client UI / persisted driver state |
| `src/types/` | Shared TS types when not colocated |
| `src/services/` | Typed HTTP/API functions (e.g. `driverEarningsService`) |
| `src/config/` | Feature flags, env (`driverDataSource.ts`, etc.) |

Use **barrel `index.ts` only** where it clearly helps imports; do not barrel everything.

## Layout / header pattern

- **Root / driver `layout.tsx`**: fonts, providers, max-width shell, safe-area-friendly container.
- **Stacked screens**: `AppHeader` — back + title (+ optional right action). Dashboard home may omit full page header; trip uses full-screen `DriverTripLifecycleView`.
- **Guards**: Prefer one guard per segment (`AuthGuard`, `VerifiedDriverGuard`) rather than duplicating checks on every page.

## Stack practices

- **Server Components by default**; `'use client'` for hooks, browser APIs, and interactive leaves.
- **TanStack Query** for server state when APIs grow; **Zustand** for cross-UI client state (trip, wallet, availability) already in use.
- **One API layer**: central fetch/axios wrapper + typed functions under `src/lib/` or `src/api/` when expanded.
- **Routes**: shared path constants in `src/lib/` (e.g. onboarding routes) to avoid string drift.

## Quality gate

- Run **ESLint** and **`next build`** before merging structural refactors.

## Do not change without product sign-off

- Trip **status machine** and allowed transitions (`src/lib/trip/tripStatus.ts`).
- **Backend contracts** for verify-otp, sockets, and assignment APIs.
